WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.374 --> 00:00:03.224
Unit five. First Aid Skills!

2
00:00:04.177 --> 00:00:07.972
Hello, everyone! I'm Nurse Bopha, your school nurse.

3
00:00:08.022 --> 00:00:11.251
Hi, Nurse Bopha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.301 --> 00:00:15.069
Today we learn about First Aid Skills. Let's go!

5
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:19.710
Assessment. Say it with me. Assessment!

6
00:00:23.232 --> 00:00:26.566
Airway. Say it with me. Airway!

7
00:00:30.065 --> 00:00:34.082
Circulation. Say it with me. Circulation!

8
00:00:37.578 --> 00:00:41.028
Shock. Say it with me. Shock!

9
00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:48.111
Splint. Say it with me. Splint!

10
00:00:51.612 --> 00:00:55.378
Pressure. Say it with me. Pressure!

11
00:00:58.908 --> 00:01:03.558
Recovery position. Say it with me. Recovery position!

12
00:01:07.052 --> 00:01:12.202
Emergency response. Say it with me. Emergency response!

13
00:01:15.694 --> 00:01:31.254
A quick assessment checks a person's airway and circulation during an emergency response. Applying pressure can help control bleeding, and a splint can support an injury. Knowing the signs of shock and the recovery position can help save a life.

14
00:01:31.304 --> 00:01:32.611
I can do that too!

15
00:01:33.615 --> 00:01:38.719
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:38.769 --> 00:01:40.016
Circulation!

17
00:01:41.306 --> 00:01:46.437
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:46.487 --> 00:01:47.986
Recovery position!

19
00:01:49.032 --> 00:01:55.237
Did you know? Applying firm pressure to a wound is one of the most effective ways to stop bleeding!

20
00:01:55.287 --> 00:01:57.176
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:57.965 --> 00:02:06.344
Think and answer. What are the first steps to take when helping someone injured?

22
00:02:06.394 --> 00:02:07.544
Great answer!

23
00:02:08.724 --> 00:02:13.468
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:13.518 --> 00:02:16.101
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

